#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A person looks at it. Three defects in the landing board — a selector matching nothing, a crop cutting the subject, a fade wrong in both directions — were invisible to a clean build, a passing suite and every gate, and were found only by rendering the page and looking."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Accessibility: measure, do not assert"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:20
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Branding: does it read as this instance?"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Contrast COMPUTED against the real ground, including the worst case a backdrop can present; a non-colour channel wherever colour carries meaning (SC 1.4.1); an accessible name on every region; keyboard and focus order. An automated pass is necessary and not sufficient — axe accepts a non-empty placeholder as an accessible name, and a CSS selector that matches nothing raises no error at all."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every user-facing string reaches the .pot; every declared locale renders without clipping or overflow; right-to-left is laid out rather than mirrored by accident. New UI is where untranslated strings enter, because nothing was stale — there was nothing there before."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Findings go back to whoever authored the choice, because the choice was theirs: a theme is picked per note by a human or an agent, and there is no mapping to correct instead. Raised, never silently fixed — a reviewer who re-themes a note has substituted their judgement for the author's without saying so."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Findings?"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:21
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Four measured passes into R_Judge — inventory, accessibility, branding, locales — each one required to MEASURE rather than assert, because an automated pass alone missed three defects a rendered look caught outright. If GW_Findings comes back yes, this lane still does not fix anything: A_RaiseFindings sends the finding back to whoever authored the theme choice, since picking it was a judgement call this lane does not get to override."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:34
#. Diagram label
msgid "Inventory what actually renders"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:50
#. Diagram label
msgid "Judge the rendered result"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Languages: extracted, rendered, and RTL"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Marks, palettes and art against the instance's own declaration rather than a remembered style. The question a downstream folio makes sharp: would this instance inherit something it did not choose?"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:33
#. Diagram label
msgid "MVP accepted"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:10
#. Diagram label
msgid "Post-MVP theme and UI review"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Raise findings against the authoring"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewed"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:15
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:13
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reviewing what the MVP actually RENDERS — accessibility, branding, languages — once stakeholders have accepted it. Post-MVP by design: choosing a theme is an authoring judgement made per note, and there is no role-to-theme mapping to check at build time. What can be reviewed is the result, and only after there is one."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single point in this process where a person looks rather than a tool measures, reached only after all four agent passes are done — so what this lane judges is the rendered whole, not any one axis in isolation. Its finding is the only thing that can send the process to A_RaiseFindings; a clean build, a passing accessibility check and a correct branding pass can each be true and still miss what only rendering and looking catches."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which themes are in use, on which surfaces, in which locales — read off the artefacts rather than the intent. A theme declared and never chosen is not in the review; a surface nobody listed is the one that ships wrong."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/theme-ui-review.bpmn:68
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
